title Saturn enters the nocturne: two studies molt in place
prompt Keaton asked to molt any documents about Saturn into New Gauge Twilight.
think The survey read every living page naming Saturn and found exactly two ABOUT it -- the classical studies saturn-in-cancer.md and saturn-in-the-9th-house.md; everything else carries Saturn in passing (the air threshold names it as the row's planet, the readings are withheld personal pages, the ledgers quote the grid). Both are plain-named living paths, so the lawful shape is the molt in place under a checkpoint rather than a mutant at a fresh stamp -- the name keeps its promises and no citer moves.
think The checkpoint landed first (walk-back b05afd0207, stamp 20260826.205521), then each page rewrote from Gauge Field into New Gauge Twilight: register only, every claim held exactly -- Cancer, Punarvasu, the 9th house; the three quiet lessons; the cup, the river, the dam become a bank; the late bloomer and the pilgrim's shrine; the first ashrama and the 9th holding up the 10th where the Sun and Mars shine; the Bhagavata's bhakti medicine; the gratitude to Parisa Yazdi in the lineage of Vic DiCara, word for word in its facts. The Twilight moves: dusk and lantern imagery from the fifteen, the pendulum's aim-then-dissolve at each lesson, calm never gloom, and Saturn read as the night witness -- the planet the register was made for.
obs Cards A (93) and A+ (97) at Field; prose witnesses GREEN; the cubist twins of both pages stand untouched beside them, as the twins' own header promises.
obs A molt in place under a checkpoint is the second shape the mitra foundation names (the W2 shape), used today for the first time since its seating -- the elder tellings stay one git show away at the walk-back.
